# Placeholder so `go:embed all:dist` compiles on a fresh clone.

`go:embed` fails the build when the embedded directory does not exist, so this
directory is committed with a `.gitkeep` and nothing else. It is **overwritten**
by a real build:

```powershell
# from the repository root
.\dev.ps1 -Package
```

That runs `npm run build` in `frontend/` and copies `frontend/dist/*` here, so
`go build ./...` produces a binary that serves the whole app (Phase 6 / E7).

**Never edit files in this directory by hand** — the next build replaces them.

When `.gitkeep` is the only file, `SPAStatus()` reports `present = false` and the
binary answers `503 ui_unavailable` for UI routes instead of pretending a
front-end exists (`docs/DECISIONS.md` D-029).
